Ten big brave army men toting carbines;
One shot himself and then there were nine.
Nine big brave army men awaiting fate;
Eight big brave army men under fiery Heaven;
The fire blinded one and then there were seven.
Seven big brave army men afeared of the phoenix;
One got burned and then there were six.
Six big brave army men trying to survive;
Rads sickened one and then there were five.
Five big brave army men contemplating war;
Four big brave army men bunking in a tree;
One had a fall and then there were three.
Three big brave army men fighting over stew;
One shot another and then there were two.
Two big brave army men starving in the sun;
One hanged himself and then there was one.
One big brave army man left all alone;
He sighed and cried, but followed the road...

OFFICIAL COMMUNIQUE: MINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, EMPIRE OF JAPAN

CONCERNING: MEDIA CLEANLINESS, OFN MEMETIC ATTACKS

Noting that it is the responsibility of the Empire of Japan to defend its neighbors from Imperialist aggression and accepting the responsibility of countering anti-Asian sentiments in cultural life;

Noting that media, including films, novels, plays, music, and other forms of art can be political channels to support or attack the ideals of Freedom, Harmony, and Unity;

Further noting that Imperialist infiltration will act to destroy Asian consciousness for the purpose of enslavement;

Ministry of Foreign Affairs states the following:

1. The American made film "Star Wars" has recently obtained an international release;
2. "Star Wars" contains pro-imperialist and anti-Japanese, and by extension anti-Asian, sentiments;
3. Kenpentai agents suspect CIA involvement in creating the film;
4. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs humbly requests the following duties from its brothers and sisters:
5. A full ban on showings of the film "Star Wars" in movie theaters and private homes;
6. Destruction of all copies within your borders;
7. A ban on discussion of the film in newspapers and on radio and television;
8. Public promotion of Asian-made films, particularly those made by Japanese and Azad Hind artists;
9. Full access of the Kenpentai to your nation to monitor your success in achieving these goals.

--END COMMUNIQUE--
